  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTION OF CRITICAL HABITATS FOR RED KNOT, MEXICO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will reduce threats to red knots in the Gulf of Santa Clara Biosphere Reserve and San Felipe through social marketing to motivate behavior change; citizen science to implement conservation actions; and education to build a broader base of supporters. The grantee will also work on capacity building with government agencies in order to develop legal protections for critical red knot habitat in the Gulf of Mexico; determine the gulf grunion spawning grounds; predict and explore thirty potential spawning beaches in the Gulf of California; develop a framework to regulate the gulf grunion fishing in the Gulf of California; and continue monitoring important red knot wintering and spring migration sites to understand its continental migratory pattern and identify other critical habitats that may contribute to its recovery.</narrative>
  </description>
